    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "DECIMAL (FLOAT) MATH\n\nDecimal nodes work on f64. A whole number wired into one is widened for you.\nSquare Root, Power, Clamp, Lerp (linear interpolation), Mean, Map Range, Round, Floor and Ceil\ncover most day-to-day needs. Lerp(a, b, t) = a + (b - a) * t, so t=0.25 is a quarter of the way.\nMap Range converts a value from one range to another (5 in 0..10 -> 50 in 0..100).",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "TRIGONOMETRY\nSin takes radians. sin(pi) is ~0 (a tiny rounding error). Number To String turns the decimal into text for Print String.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          950.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1260.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.55,
          0.15,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "pi",
          "s",
          "txt",
          "show"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "Each result is stored into a variable by a Set node: sqrt 4, power 1024, clamp 10, lerp 25, mean 4, map-range 50, round 3, floor 2, ceil 3.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -70.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1260.0,
          90.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      }
    ],
